# An `import` inside a documentation fence is not an import

THIS IS THE CONTROL, and it fails loudly rather than silently: the module named below DOES NOT
EXIST, so if the scanner ever stops caring which fence a line sits in, `Loader.resolve` throws
`cannot find the import 'std/no-such-module.ssc'` and this file stops running.

Written because the standard library already contains four such lines — `std/actors.ssc` and
`std/nodes.ssc` each show `import actors.ChildSpec` in a ```` ```text ```` block — and every one
of them happens to name its OWN file, so reading them as imports would have been a harmless no-op
that nothing could have detected.

```text
import no_such_module.Thing
```

```scalascript
println("doc fence is prose")
```
